course: dictionary
lesson: 13191
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context, the words around them, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Mum sliced the fruitcake and gave everyone a piece at Christmas.» The clues are sliced, Christmas and gave, so fruitcake is the food.
explain: «Dad said Uncle Tom was nutty as a fruitcake when he wore a Santa hat to the shops in July.» Nobody is eating anything here. Nutty as a fruitcake means very silly or odd, so the clues point to the second meaning. Ask yourself: does the sentence make sense with a cake, or with a person?
explain: The second meaning is slang, and it can be unkind, so do not use it to call people names. Some people with mental illness are hurt by this word. Use the food meaning when you talk about cake, and be careful with the slang.
fact: A fruitcake is a rich cake full of dried fruit, like raisins, currants and cherries.
fact: «Fruitcake» often means the food, and it is often eaten at Christmas and weddings.
fact: As slang, «fruitcake» means a person who seems crazy or very strange.
fact: «Nutty as a fruitcake» means very silly or mad.
fact: Some words have one meaning in a cake shop and a different meaning in everyday talk. Context tells you which one to use.
exercise: «Grandma baked a fruitcake full of raisins, currants and cherries.» What is a fruitcake here? | A fruit bowl on the kitchen table | *A rich cake full of dried fruit | A small bird that sings in the morning | A bread roll with no sugar
exercise: Which word is a clue that «fruitcake» means food in «Every slice of fruitcake tasted sweet»? | Silly | Nutty | Every | *tasted
exercise: Jo says, «Our neighbour is nutty as a fruitcake, he talks to his hedge.» What does nutty as a fruitcake mean? | *Very strange or silly | Hungry for cake | Good at baking | A type of nut
test: «We cut the fruitcake at the wedding.» What is the fruitcake? | A pile of nuts | A bird that sings at weddings | *A rich cake full of dried fruit | A person who acts crazy
test: What does calling someone a fruitcake mean, as slang? | A person who likes fruit | A baker who makes cakes | A party guest | *Someone who seems odd or crazy
exam: Which sentence uses fruitcake as food? | «That fruitcake is totally bonkers.» | *«We ate a slice of fruitcake after dinner.» | «The fruitcake was shouting at the bus.»
